1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,739
You've been writing leads,

2
00:00:02,189 --> 00:00:04,363
and a lead happens once.

3
00:00:05,263 --> 00:00:08,741
Today you write the other kind of quest,

4
00:00:09,191 --> 00:00:13,104
the kind a crew can take again and again.

5
00:00:14,904 --> 00:00:20,557
That's what a job is: a station offers it, the crew takes it,

6
00:00:21,007 --> 00:00:23,615
they do it, and they're paid.

7
00:00:24,515 --> 00:00:27,993
And when they come back, it's there again.

8
00:00:29,193 --> 00:00:33,541
Here's the whole life of a job, in five stages.

9
00:00:34,441 --> 00:00:41,833
First it's offered, when Comms selects a station, and each job is a button, with its pay.

10
00:00:43,633 --> 00:00:49,720
Then it's taken, and it goes into the Quest Log, under the ship's name.

11
00:00:50,620 --> 00:00:54,098
Then it's done, when its ending comes true,

12
00:00:54,548 --> 00:00:57,157
wherever the ship happens to be.

13
00:00:58,957 --> 00:01:05,043
Then it's paid, in credits, and in standing with the side that offered it.

14
00:01:05,943 --> 00:01:08,117
And then it's offered again.

15
00:01:09,917 --> 00:01:12,961
Now, the template gave you three jobs,

16
00:01:13,411 --> 00:01:17,324
and two of them have no ending at all.

17
00:01:18,224 --> 00:01:22,137
A crew can take them, and never finish them.

18
00:01:23,337 --> 00:01:26,380
An ending is one line, Done when,

19
00:01:26,830 --> 00:01:31,178
and it's an order to the captain in plain words.

20
00:01:32,978 --> 00:01:35,152
There are five first words.

21
00:01:36,052 --> 00:01:38,661
Destroy. Recover. Scan. Reach. And dock.

22
00:01:39,561 --> 00:01:43,909
After the word comes a number, and what to count.

23
00:01:45,709 --> 00:01:49,187
So, for Patrol: Done when, destroy three enemies.

24
00:01:50,087 --> 00:01:53,130
Enemies is a word the game knows.

25
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:57,059
It means anything at war with the crew.

26
00:01:58,859 --> 00:02:04,511
And the game shows that same line to the crew as their objective,

27
00:02:04,961 --> 00:02:08,439
so write it the way you'd say it.

28
00:02:09,639 --> 00:02:11,813
Salvage is the Gleaners' job.

29
00:02:12,713 --> 00:02:15,322
Its ending is, recover two tech,

30
00:02:15,772 --> 00:02:19,685
and tech is a key from your Goods chapter.

31
00:02:21,485 --> 00:02:23,659
Now look at the reward.

32
00:02:24,559 --> 00:02:27,602
After the credits I'm adding a comma,

33
00:02:28,052 --> 00:02:33,270
and then a deed, the same three words as in Lecture Four.

34
00:02:34,170 --> 00:02:37,213
A side, a trait, and a number.

35
00:02:39,013 --> 00:02:42,926
So this job pays, and it pleases the Gleaners.

36
00:02:43,826 --> 00:02:47,304
But the farmers hear who's been stripping wrecks,

37
00:02:47,754 --> 00:02:51,667
and they think a little less of the crew.

38
00:02:53,467 --> 00:02:55,207
And mind that comma.

39
00:02:55,657 --> 00:02:59,135
Leave it out, and the credits are paid,

40
00:02:59,585 --> 00:03:04,802
the deed is dropped, and lint gives you a warning about it.

41
00:03:06,002 --> 00:03:07,741
Three more jobs, quickly.

42
00:03:08,641 --> 00:03:12,989
A survey, which ends when Science scans a dead ship.

43
00:03:14,789 --> 00:03:17,398
A run home, against the clock.

44
00:03:18,298 --> 00:03:20,037
Fails when, ten minutes,

45
00:03:20,487 --> 00:03:23,096
and a penalty if it does.

46
00:03:23,996 --> 00:03:27,909
You know both of those lines from Class One.

47
00:03:29,709 --> 00:03:32,317
And a strike, at tier three.

48
00:03:33,217 --> 00:03:38,000
That one's only offered to a crew the Compact really trusts.

49
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:43,278
The relay run does something else for me.

50
00:03:44,178 --> 00:03:45,917
It ends at home,

51
00:03:46,367 --> 00:03:49,411
so it's a way back that pays.

52
00:03:50,611 --> 00:03:53,654
A job nobody offers is never seen.

53
00:03:54,554 --> 00:03:57,163
So, back up to the sides.

54
00:03:58,963 --> 00:04:02,007
The farmers get patrol, escort and strike.

55
00:04:02,907 --> 00:04:06,820
The miners get the survey and the relay run.

56
00:04:08,620 --> 00:04:12,098
I'm taking the escort away from the miners,

57
00:04:12,548 --> 00:04:16,026
because it ends at their own front door.

58
00:04:16,926 --> 00:04:19,970
A job that ends at a place

59
00:04:20,420 --> 00:04:23,898
belongs to a side that lives somewhere else.

60
00:04:25,098 --> 00:04:27,707
I save, and lint says clean.

61
00:04:29,507 --> 00:04:32,985
And today that's less than half the check.

62
00:04:33,885 --> 00:04:36,493
Lint knows the five first words,

63
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:39,987
so a misspelled one gets a warning.

64
00:04:40,887 --> 00:04:43,930
But it doesn't read what comes after.

65
00:04:45,730 --> 00:04:48,339
Write the number as a word,

66
00:04:48,789 --> 00:04:50,963
and the job never finishes.

67
00:04:51,863 --> 00:04:56,211
Name a good you don't have, and it never finishes.

68
00:04:58,011 --> 00:05:01,489
And here's the one that will catch you.

69
00:05:02,389 --> 00:05:04,998
You can't write, destroy three gleaners.

70
00:05:05,898 --> 00:05:08,507
The game takes the s off,

71
00:05:08,957 --> 00:05:12,870
looks for something called a gleaner, and finds nothing.

72
00:05:13,770 --> 00:05:15,509
So write enemies instead.

73
00:05:16,709 --> 00:05:19,752
At home, the farmers offer one job.

74
00:05:20,652 --> 00:05:22,391
I pay the levy,

75
00:05:22,841 --> 00:05:27,189
and now there are two, and the escort pays more.

76
00:05:28,989 --> 00:05:33,772
I take both, and here they are in the Quest Log.

77
00:05:34,672 --> 00:05:38,585
I engage the escort, and on arrival it's done.

78
00:05:40,385 --> 00:05:43,863
The miners' office has my two new jobs.

79
00:05:44,763 --> 00:05:49,980
I take them, and the clock on the relay run is running.

80
00:05:51,780 --> 00:05:54,389
The survey wants a dead ship,

81
00:05:54,839 --> 00:05:57,448
and I know where one is.

82
00:05:58,348 --> 00:06:00,522
And the patrol wants enemies,

83
00:06:00,972 --> 00:06:04,015
and I know where those are too.

84
00:06:05,215 --> 00:06:08,259
The Gleaners will deal with me now,

85
00:06:08,709 --> 00:06:10,883
so I take their salvage.

86
00:06:12,683 --> 00:06:15,291
When it's done, watch the farmers.

87
00:06:16,191 --> 00:06:18,800
My standing with them just dropped,

88
00:06:19,250 --> 00:06:21,859
and I never spoke to them.

89
00:06:23,659 --> 00:06:28,441
Now the relay run takes me home, inside its ten minutes.

90
00:06:29,341 --> 00:06:31,950
And look at the farmers' list.

91
00:06:32,850 --> 00:06:38,067
Patrol is back, and it pays a little more than last time.

92
00:06:39,867 --> 00:06:43,346
That's the thing to remember about a job.

93
00:06:44,246 --> 00:06:45,985
It never runs out.

94
00:06:46,885 --> 00:06:53,841
So think about how often you want a crew to be able to please each side.

95
00:06:55,041 --> 00:06:56,780
Now it's your turn.

96
00:06:57,680 --> 00:07:02,898
Write one job for each side that only that side would offer.

97
00:07:03,798 --> 00:07:06,407
Make one of them tier two.

98
00:07:06,857 --> 00:07:10,335
Make one that costs the crew somewhere else.

99
00:07:11,235 --> 00:07:16,017
And put one against the clock, and let it fail once.

100
00:07:17,817 --> 00:07:20,861
Next time, your universe gets a story,

101
00:07:21,311 --> 00:07:23,920
with a beginning and an end.
